{%- comment -%}
  The type of a selling plan, by selling plan ID: "60-day" or "year", its Duos per delivery and, for a
  year plan, the year total the checkout must charge. This is the only table of plan IDs in the theme.
  Plan logic keys on the type, never on plan or group names, so renaming or translating a plan changes
  nothing:
  - the "Subscription Name" for Care Credit (snippets/kc-plan-loyalty.liquid)
  - the billing interval, deliveries and Dental Check-up Reward (assets/kc-plan-select.js PLAN_TYPES)
  - the Duos per delivery: the cart quantity of the plan and the prices shown for it
    (snippets/kc-plan-config.liquid, assets/kc-plan-select.js units())
  - the end CTA interval and price (sections/featured-product.liquid), the sticky bar price
    (snippets/sticky-cart-block.liquid) and the cart quantity lock (snippets/cart-drawer.liquid,
    sections/main-cart-items.liquid; neither is rendered while the theme has no cart, layout/theme.liquid)
  It lists every selling plan of the product, the legacy email offers included (they never show on the
  product page, but any theme path that adds them gets the same treatment).

  Year plan: 3 Duos per delivery, 2 deliveries (now and month 6), paid up front: 6 Duos x €59 = €354.
  Cart quantity = Duos per delivery = 3.
  Shopify's price per quantity is a year price (€118, admin only), never a per-Duo price:
  €118 x 3 = €354. Do not compare it with the Duos in one delivery.

  Duos per delivery: 60-day plans 1; year plans the theme setting "Year plans: Duos per delivery"
  (settings.kc_year_units_per_delivery: 3, or 1 as an emergency rollback); an unknown plan 1
  (kc-plan-config warns in the theme editor, kc-plan-select.js on the storefront).

  Expected year total (in cents, shop currency) while year plans are 3 Duos per delivery: a safety
  check only, never displayed. kc-plan-config and kc-plan-select.js warn when Shopify's year price per
  quantity x quantity differs:
  354.00 = 6 x 59 (The Karmicare Year and the swapped Subscribe and Save plan),
  294.00 = 6 x 49 (Yearly Plan and the first year of Subscribe and Save 49 -> 59).

  Deliveries per billing: 60-day plans 1, year plans 2 (paid for the year, delivered now and in month 6;
  the same as PLAN_TYPES in assets/kc-plan-select.js). A year plan holds units x 2 Duos a year.

  Care Credit per order, in %: 60-day plans 10 ("Care Credit - 10%" in Loop Loyalty, Subscription Name
  "60-Day Supply"), year plans 20 ("Care Credit - 20%", "Year Supply"), an unknown plan 0 (no
  Subscription Name). The preview where no duos metaobject value applies (end CTA, buybox fallback).

  Accepts:
  - plan_id: {String|Number} a selling plan ID
  - field: {String} 'type' (default), 'units', 'deliveries', 'expected_total' or 'care_credit_percent'

  Outputs, by field: "60-day", "year" or nothing for an unknown plan; the Duos per delivery (1 for an
  unknown plan); the deliveries per billing (1 for an unknown plan); the expected year total in cents,
  or nothing; the Care Credit % (0 for an unknown plan).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  # 60-day: 60-Day Rhythm, 60-Day Supply, Subscribe and Save "Deliver every 60 days".
  # Year: The Karmicare Year, Yearly Plan, both Subscribe and Save "Pay every 12 months" plans.
  assign kc_wanted = plan_id | append: '' | remove: 'gid://shopify/SellingPlan/' | strip
  assign kc_type = ''
  assign kc_units = 1
  assign kc_deliveries = 1
  assign kc_expected_total = ''
  assign kc_care_credit_percent = 0
  assign kc_year_units = settings.kc_year_units_per_delivery | default: 3 | plus: 0
  case kc_wanted
    when '712106115453', '712192164221', '712387297661'
      assign kc_type = '60-day'
      assign kc_care_credit_percent = 10
    when '712155431293', '712387363197'
      assign kc_type = 'year'
      assign kc_units = kc_year_units
      assign kc_deliveries = 2
      assign kc_expected_total = '35400'
      assign kc_care_credit_percent = 20
    when '712370356605', '712387330429'
      assign kc_type = 'year'
      assign kc_units = kc_year_units
      assign kc_deliveries = 2
      assign kc_expected_total = '29400'
      assign kc_care_credit_percent = 20
  endcase

  case field
    when 'units'
      echo kc_units
    when 'deliveries'
      echo kc_deliveries
    when 'expected_total'
      echo kc_expected_total
    when 'care_credit_percent'
      echo kc_care_credit_percent
    else
      echo kc_type
  endcase
-%}
